@startuml
title Recommendation request — session and retrieval decisions
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox

actor User
participant RequestGateway as Gateway
participant AiInputParser as Parser
participant SessionTransitionService as Transition
participant "ConversationEngine\nIntent handlers + RecommendationPager" as Engine
participant "SessionRepository\nRedis adapter" as Sessions
participant "RecommendationWorkflow\nEmbedding → retrieval → ranking" as Workflow
participant "ConversationResponseGenerator\nAI narration when needed" as Response

User -> Gateway : Natural-language request
Gateway -> Parser : Parse intent, criteria and count
Parser --> Gateway : Parsed request
note over Parser
  Only RECOMMENDATION and REFINE accept
  new semantic criteria.
  Parser and response chat models can differ.
end note
Gateway -> Transition : Process request
Transition -> Sessions : update(sessionId, userId, change)
activate Sessions
note over Sessions
  Acquire session lock.
  Load session and run the transition.
end note
Sessions -> Transition : Apply change to loaded session
activate Transition
Transition -> Engine : Resolve, validate and complete the turn
activate Engine

alt REPEAT
  Engine -> Engine : Restore last completed request outcome\nKeep pending queue unchanged
else Explanation or repeat recommendations
  Engine -> Engine : Reuse displayed page or saved outcome\nNo candidate retrieval
else MORE with no previous search
  Engine -> Engine : Mark search clarification required\nDo not retrieve candidates
else Recommendation, refinement, or MORE
  Engine -> Engine : Intent handler resolves context and preferences\nDiscard stale queue if search changed
  Engine -> Engine : Take pending recommendations, up to requested count
  opt Page still needs books
    Engine -> Workflow : Build fresh batch, excluding shown IDs and cached tail
    activate Workflow
    Workflow -> Workflow : Load user preference vectors\nBuild query vectors when needed
    alt Personalised request lacks usable preferences
      Workflow --> Engine : Ask for taste preferences
    else Search can proceed
      Workflow -> Workflow : Retrieve up to 50 candidates\nRank up to 20 recommendations
      Workflow --> Engine : New batch for session queue
    end
    deactivate Workflow
    Engine -> Engine : Fill page from new queue\nReturn fewer if necessary
  end
  Engine -> Engine : Handler completes action; history records the turn\nEmpty MORE = no further matches
else Count, preference, history, help or unknown action
  Engine -> Engine : Apply the relevant session action\nNo candidate retrieval
end

Engine --> Transition : Completed ConversationTurn
deactivate Engine
Transition --> Sessions : Transition result
deactivate Transition
Sessions -> Sessions : Commit session if lock and version still match\nKeep lease held and renewed
Sessions -> Gateway : Run afterCommit with selected page and decision
Gateway -> Response : Generate wording using resolved decision and context
note over Response
  Chat model for book explanations.
  Built-in wording for actions, clarification,
  exhausted results and model failures.
end note
Response --> Gateway : Response text
Gateway --> Sessions : Generated response
Sessions -> Sessions : Release session lease
Sessions --> Transition : Completed request
Transition --> Gateway : Generated response
deactivate Sessions
Gateway --> User : Response
note over Gateway, Sessions
  Commit precedes final response generation.
  Busy lock: 409. Lost lock or rejected commit: 503.
end note
@enduml
